      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "WHY. Why remove support for a controller that belongs to a headset that is still used today?!\n\nI literally use the vive wands often still as an index controller owner as they're great for gestures, and another big reason I prefer the vive wands is because my hands are too small to use the index controllers and get good finger tracking, i cant even reliably make most of the gestures, my fingers are too short. \n\nplus with the vive wands you can even rebind other gestures to the trigger and use gesture weight on them which has always been cool and was something only exclusive to the vive wands as far as I'm aware, which you can't do on index.\n\n Just why??? Big L",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
